"Thomas J. Waisanen" <tjwais@umich.edu> writes:

> I'm an explvl 22 wiz who is ABOUT to ascend for the first time. I'm
> hanging out on DL 1 with the amulet, good HP, good SP, good AC (-48)
> with all the right armor, spells a-N and most of the good ones
> castable, enchanted frostbrand and magicbane, and pretty much
> everything else I think I'd need or want. However, I still have a WoW
> at (1:2), so I have 3 wishes left. What do y'all receommend would be
> useful? Maybe a magic marker or two, to get cursed scrolls of genocide
> for wraiths or nurses? Or an amulet of life saving (I currently do NOT
> have one...)? 

Assuming you have the standard stuff, yes, Amulet of life saving is 
indeed of great value, in particular for the first time.  Also, a 
wand of death is very handy for some real scary guys you'll meet 
on the astral plane.  (For a Wizard, Finger of Death is more 
stylish, of course, hence if you don't know it, wish for a spellbook 
of Finger of Death.)  Next, you should carry remove curse and 
some scrolls of gold detection with you.  Finally, it is highly 
advisable to have rings of free action, conflict and levitation 
at hand.  Ah, and 4-5 wands of digging are useful.  

> Any other advice for me before I go up to the planes
> would be greatly appreciated. 

- Go through the elemental planes fast.  Locate the portal 
  and go for it.   Ah, you might need some potions of full 
  healing on the plane of air; the air elementals are strong.  
  Alchemize some.  Again, keep going; Rodney follows you to 
  the elemental planes, and the planes have nothing of 
  interest to you.  

- Wear conflict on the air plane, it slows 
  down the speed the air elementals come after you.  The rest 
  of the time free action is best.  Second ring is levitation.  
  I never used conflict on the astral plane, hence I 
  can't say whether it's a good idea.  

- On astral plane, the first thing to do is to kill all 
  major liches on the plane.  Don't proceed before that 
  is done.  (Check with a blindfold.)  

- Archons are annoying and well worth a death ray.  
  But keep some rays for the riders.  

- Don't get too near to krakens, and be very scared of 
  (master) mind flayers.  

- If the riders get too annoying, you can trap them with 
  scrolls of earth.  (Can they be tamed?  Never tried.)

- If you're standing on the correct altar, amulet in hands, 
  and feel the urge to clean the astral plane first, DON'T 
  DO THAT, NO, REALLY, JUST OFFER THE ROTTEN AMULET AND BE 
  DONE!

